==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Znache]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zroco]]s spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 3.33~13.33 seconds<sup>100f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zomboe]]s spawn after 86.67 seconds<sup>2,600f</sup>, delay 30~60 seconds<sup>900f~1,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zigge]]s spawn after 86.67 seconds<sup>2,600f</sup>, delay 30~60 seconds<sup>900f~1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Zang Roo]] spawns after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Zang Roo]] spawns after 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Kang Roo]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 70% HP:
**1 [[Kang Roo]] spawns.

==Strategy==
You have a bit of time to upgrade your [[Worker Cat]] with the early flood of peons. Damaging the enemy base will summon a couple of Kang Roos for you to deal with. If you take a while before getting to the base, you may have to fight a Zang Roo and a Kang Roo at the same time, so it may be better to wait before hitting the base in order to lure out the Zang Roos first so you can deal with the Kang Roos freely. Note that Zigge and Zomboe will spawn as well and have to be dealt with if you are luring out all the Zang Roos.

Zang Roo can easily kill your newly spawned units if you don't have enough ranged attackers to deal with her, so still do be careful.

